hadiths[82]{hadithnumber,text}:
"630","Yahya related to me that Malik had seen that the people of knowledge used to like to pay the zakat al-fitr after dawn had broken on the day of the Fitr before they went to the place of prayer. Malik said"
"631","Yahya related to me from Malik from Abdullah ibn Dinar from Abdullah ibn Umar that the Messenger of Allah"
"632","Yahya related to me from Malik from Thawr ibn Zayd ad-Dili from Abdullah ibn Abbas that the Messenger of Allah"
"633","Yahya related to me from Malik that he had heard that once in the time of Uthman ibn Affan the new moon had been seen in the afternoon and Uthman did not break his fast until evening had come and the sun had set. Yahya said that he had heard Malik say that some one who sees the new moon of Ramadan when he is on his own should start the fast and not break it if he knows that that day is part of Ramadan. He added"
"634","Yahya related to me from Malik from Nafi that Abdullah ibn Umar used to say"
"635","Yahya related to me from Malik from Ibn Shihab that A'isha and Hafsa"
"636","Yahya related to me from Malik from Abu Hazim ibn Dinar from Sahl ibn Sad as Saidi that the Messenger of Allah"
"637","Yahya related to me from Malik from Abd ar-Rahman ibn Harmala al- Aslami from Said ibn al-Musayyab that the Messenger of Allah"
"638","Yahya related to me from Malik from Ibn Shihab from Humayd ibn Abd ar-Rahman that Umar ibn al-Khattab and Uthman ibn Affan would pray maghrib when they saw the night darkening"
"639","Yahya related to me from Malik from Abdullah ibn Abd ar-Rahman ibn Mamar al-Ansari from Abu Yunus"
"640","Yahya related to me from Malik from Abd Rabbih ibn Said from Abu Bakr ibn Abd ar-Rahman ibn al-Harith ibn Hisham from A'isha and Umm Salama"
"641","Yahya related to me from Malik from Sumayy"
"642","Yahya related to me from Malik from Sumayy"
"643","Yahya related to me from Malik from Zayd ibn Aslam from Ata ibn Yasar that a certain man kissed his wife while he was fasting in Ramadan. This made him very anxious"
"644","Yahya related to me from Malik from Hisham ibn Urwa from his father that A'isha"
"645","Yahya related to me from Malik from Yahya ibn Said that Atika bint Zayd ibn Amr ibn Nufayl"
"646","Yahya related to me from Malik from Abu'n-Nadr"
"647","Yahya related to me from Malik from Zayd ibn Aslam that Abu Hurayra and Sad ibn Abi Waqqas used to say that someone who was fasting was allowed to kiss"
"648","Yahya related to me from Malik that he had heard that A'isha"
"649","Yahya said that Malik said that Hisham ibn Urwa ibn az-Zubayr had said"
"650","Yahya related to me from Malik from Zayd ibn Aslam from Ata ibn Yasar that Abdullah ibn Abbas was asked about people kissing while fasting and he said that he allowed it for old men but disapproved of it for young men"
"651","Yahya related to me from Malik from Nafi that Abdullah ibn Umar used to forbid kissing and fondling for people who were fasting"
"652","Yahya related to me from Malik from Ibn Shihab from Ubaydullah ibn Abdullah ibn Utba ibn Masud from Abdullah ibn Abbas that the Messenger of Allah"
"653","Yahya related to me from Malik from Sumayy"
"654","Yahya related to me from Malik from Humayd at-Tawil that Anas ibn Malik said"
"655","Yahya related to me from Malik from Hisham ibn Urwa from his father that Hamza ibn Amr al-Aslami once said to the Messenger of Allah"
"656","Yahya related to me from Malik from Nafi that Abdullah ibn Umar used not to fast while travelling"
"657","Yahya related to me from Malik that Hisham ibn Urwa said"
"658","Yahya related to me from Malik that he had heard that Umar ibn al-Khattab"
"659","Yahya related to me from Malik from Ibn Shihab from Hunayd ibn Abd arRahman ibn Awf from Abu Hurayra that a man broke the fast in Ramadan and the Messenger of Allah"
"660","Yahya related to me from Malik from Ata ibn Abdullah al-Khurasani that Said ibn al-Musayyab said"
"661","Malik said"
"662","Yahya related to me from Malik from Ibn Shihab that Sad ibn Abi Waqqas and Abdullah ibn Umar used to be cupped while they were fasting"
"663","Yahya related to me from Malik from Hisham ibn Urwa that his father used to be cupped while he was fasting and he would not then break his fast. Hisham added"
"664","Yahya related to me from Malik from Hisham ibn Urwa from his father that A'isha"
"665","Yahya related to me from Malik from Ibn Shihab that Humayd ibn Abd ar-Rahman ibn Awf heard Muawiya ibn Abi Sufyan say from the mimbar on the day of Ashura in the year in which he made the hajj"
"666","Yahya related to me from Malik that he had heard that Umar ibn al-Khattab had sent (the following message) to al-Harith ibn Hisham"
"667","Yahya related to me from Malik from Muhammad ibn Yahya ibn Habban from alAraj from Abu Hurayra that the Messenger of Allah"
"668","Yahya related to me from Malik that he used to hear the people of knowledge say"
"669","Yahya related to me from Malik from Nafi from Abdullah ibn Umar that the Messenger of Allah"
"670","Yahya related to me from Malik from Abu'z-Zinad from al-Araj from Abu Hurayra that the Messenger of Allah"
"673","Hadith Translation Not available"
"674","Yahya related to me from Malik from Zayd ibn Aslam from his brother Khalid ibn Aslam that Umar ibn al-Khattab once broke thefast on a cloudy day thinking that evening had come and the sun had set. Then a man came to him and said"
"675","Yahya related to me from Malik from Nafi that Abdullah ibn Umar used to say"
"676","Yahya related to me from Malik from Ibr Shihab that Abdullah ibn Abbas and Abu Hurayra differed about making up days missed in Ramadan. One of them said that they were done separately and the other said that they were done consecutively. He did not know which one of them it was who said that they were done separately"
"677","Yahya related to me from Malik from Nafi that Abdullah ibn Umar used to say"
"678","Yahya related to me from Malik from Yahya ibn Said that he heard Said ibn al Musayyab being asked about making up days missed in Ramadan"
"679","Yahya related to me from Malik that Humayd ibn Oays al-Makki told him"
"680","Yahya related to me from Malik from Ibn Shihab that A'isha and Hafsa"
"681","Yahya said that he heard Malik say"
"682","Yahya related to me from Malik that he had heard that Abdullah ibn Umar was asked about what a pregnant woman should do if the fast became difficult for her and she feared for her child"
"683","Yahya related to me from Malik from Abd ar-Rahman ibn al-Qasim that his father used to say"
"685","Yahya related to me from Malik from Yahya ibn Said from Abu Salama ibn Abd ar-Rahman that he heard A'isha"
"686","Yahya related to me from Malik that he had heard the people of knowledge telling people not to fast on the day in Shaban when there was doubt (about whether it was Shaban or Ramadan)"
"687","Yahya related to me from Malik from Abu'z Zinad from al-A'raj from Abu Hurayra that the Messenger of Allah"
"688","Yahya related to me from Malik from Abu'z Zinad from al-Araj from Abu Hurayra that the Messenger of Allah"
"689","Yahya related to me from Malik from his paternal uncle Abu Suhayl ibn Malik from his father that Abu Hurayra said"
"690","Yahya related to me from Malik that he had heard that the people of knowledge did not disapprove of people fasting using tooth-sticks at any hour of the day in Ramadan"
"691","Yahya related to me from Malik from Ibn Shihab from Amra bint Abd ar-Rahman that when A'isha was doing itikaf she would only ask after sick people if she was walking and not if she was standing still. Malik said"
"692","Yahya related to me from Malik that he had asked Ibn Shihab whether someone doing itikaf could go into a house to relieve himself"
"693","Yahya related to me from Malik that he had heard that al-Qasim ibn Muhammad and Nafi"
"696","Malik was asked whether someone who went into a mosque to do itikaf for the last ten days of Ramadan and stayed there for a day or two but then became ill and left the mosque"
"697","Malik said"
"698","Ziyad related to me from Malik from Hisham ibn Urwa from his father that the Messenger of Allah"
"699","Ziyad related to me from Malik from Abdullah ibn Dinar from Abdullah ibn Umar that the Messenger of Allah"
"700","Ziyad related to me from Malik from Abu'n Nadr"
"701","Ziyad related to me from Malik from Humayd at-Tawil that 'Anas ibn Malik said"
"702","Ziyad related to me from Malik from Nafi from Ibn 'Umar that some of the companions of the Messenger of Allah"
"703","Ziyad related to me from Malik that he had heard a man he trusted of the people of knowledge say"
"704","Ziyad related to me from Malik that he had heard that Said ibn al-Musayyab used to say"
"705","Yahya related to me from Malik from Abd ar-Rahman ibn al-Qasim from his father from Asma bint Umays that she gave birth to Muhammad ibn Abi Bakr at al-Bayda. Abu Bakr mentioned this to the Messenger of Allah"
"706","Yahya related to me from Malik from Yahya ibn Said from Said ibn al-Musayyab that Asma bint Umays gave birth to Muhammad ibn Abi Bakr at Dhu'l-Hulayfa and Abu Bakr told her to do ghusl and then enter ihram"
"707","Yahya related to me from Malik from Nafi' that 'Abdullah ibn Umar used to do ghusl for ihram before he entered ihram"
"708","Yahya related to me from Malik from Zayd ibn Aslam from Ibrahim ibn Abdullah ibn Hunayn from his father Abdullah ibn Hunayn that Abdullah ibn Abbas and al-Miswar ibn Makhrama once had a disagreement at al-Abwa. Abdullah said that some one in ihram could wash his head"
"709","Malik related to me from Humayd ibn Qays from Ata ibn Abi Rabah that 'Umar ibn alKhattab once asked Yala ibn Munya"
"710","Malik related to me from Nafi that Abdullah ibn Umar would spend the night between the two trails in the valley of Dhu Tuwa when he was approaching Makka. Then he would pray subh"
"711","Yahya related to me from Malik from Nafi that Abdullah ibn Umar would never wash his head while he was in ihram except if he had to do ghusl because of a wet dream. Malik said"
"712","Yahya related to me from Malik from Nafi from Abdullah ibn Umar that a man once asked the Messenger of Allah"
"713","Yahya related to me from Malik from 'Abdullah ibn Dinar that Abdullah ibn Umar said"
"714","Yahya related to me from Malik from Nafi that he had heard Aslam"
"715","Yahya related to me from Malik from Hisham ibn Urwa from his father that Asma bint Abi Bakr had worn clothes that were completely dyed with safflower while she was in ihram"
"716","Yahya related to me from Malik from Nafi that 'Abdullah ibn 'Umar used to disapprove of anybody wearing a belt or girdle while in ihram"